<title>CHILE: Chilean copper exports fall in August.</title>
<headline>Chilean copper exports fall in August.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper exports fell to $487 million in August from $662 million in the same month of 1995 and $580 million in July, Central Bank reported.</p>
<p>Total mining sector exports fell to $586 million in August from $766 million in August last year.</p>
<p>Mining exports reported by the Central Bank in August were as follows, in millions of dollars, with August 1995 figures in parentheses:</p>
<p>    Copper -		 487  (662)</p>
<p>    Iron -		    15  (18)</p>
<p>Nitrates and iodine - 10  (9)</p>
<p>    Silver -		  12  (12)</p>
<p>    Molybdenum -	    15  (27)</p>
<p>    Lithium carbonate -    3  (3)</p>
<p>Gold, metallic</p>
<p>     and dore metal -     34  (29)</p>
<p>    Gold minerals -	  0  (-0.1)</p>
<p>    Other -		   10  (5)</p>
<p>    TOTAL -		  586  (765)</p>
<p>--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
</text>
